<title>USA: CME board names Melamed as senior policy adviser.</title>
<headline>CME board names Melamed as senior policy adviser.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Chicago Mercantile Exchange said Thursday its board named Leo Melamed as senior policy adviser.</p>
<p>The board late Wednesday re-instituted the position, which was created in 1989 and pays $200,000 a year. Current CME chairman Jack Sandner held the paid post in 1989 and 1990.</p>
<p>Melamed, who became CME chairman emeritus in 1991, was named permanent adviser to the board at a January 22 organizational meeting.</p>
<p>He is chairman and chief executive officer of Sakura Dellsher Inc, a CME clearing member firm.</p>
